\begin{aligned}
& \mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{CH}_2 \mathrm{CH}_2 \mathrm{CH}_2 \mathrm{NH}_2 \stackrel{\mathrm{CHCl}_3+\text { alc } \mathrm{KOH}}{\longrightarrow} \\
& \mathrm{CH}_3\left(\mathrm{CH}_2\right)_3 \mathrm{NC} \\
& \text { bad smelling } \\
&
\end{aligned}

(B) Terminal alkynes like $\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{C} \equiv \mathrm{CH}$ give white precipitate with ammoniacal $\mathrm{AgNO}_3$.

\begin{array}{r}
\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{C} \equiv \mathrm{CH}+\mathrm{AgNO}_3+\mathrm{NH}_4 \mathrm{OH} \longrightarrow \\
\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{C} \equiv \mathrm{CAg} \\
\text { white ppt }
\end{array}

(C) Ester $\left(\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{CH}_2 \mathrm{COOCH}_3\right)$ undergoes alkaline hydrolysis.

\begin{array}{r}
\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{CH}_2 \mathrm{COOCH}_3+\mathrm{NaOH} \longrightarrow \\
\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{CH}_2 \mathrm{COONa}+\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{OH}
\end{array}

(D) $2^{\circ}$ alcohols (the alcohols that have $\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{CHOH}$ - group) give cloudiness with Lucas reagent (anhy $\mathrm{ZnCl}_2+$ conc $\mathrm{HCl}$ ) within 5 minutes.

The charring of sugar is its dehydration process. When sugar is treated with conc. $\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{SO}_4$, water molecules gets escaped and sugar charcoal is formed. Due to its further reaction with acid, smell of $\mathrm{SO}_2$ is obtained.

\begin{array}{rl}
\mathrm{C}_{12} \mathrm{H}_{22} \mathrm{O}_{11}+\left[\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{SO}_4\right] & \longrightarrow \\
\text { Sugar } & 12 \mathrm{C}+\left[\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}+\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{SO}_4\right] \\
& \text { Sugar charcoal } \\
\mathrm{C}+2 \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{SO}_4 & 2 \mathrm{SO}_2+\mathrm{CO}_2+2 \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}
\end{array}

$\mathrm{PCl}_5$ on reaction with alcohol and carboxylic acid, replace $-\mathrm{OH}$ group with $-\mathrm{Cl}$.

\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{ROH}+\mathrm{PCl}_5 \longrightarrow \mathrm{RCl} & +\mathrm{POCl}_3+\mathrm{HCl} \\
\mathrm{RCOOH}+\mathrm{PCl}_5 \longrightarrow & \mathrm{RCOCl}^2 \\
+ & \mathrm{POCl}_3+\mathrm{HCl}
\end{aligned}

