\begin{aligned}
& \mathrm{E}_{\mathrm{y}}=2.5 \frac{\mathrm{N}}{\mathrm{C}} \cos \left[\left(2 \pi \times 10^6 \frac{\mathrm{rad}}{\mathrm{m}}\right) \mathrm{t}\right. \\
&\left.-\left(\pi \times 10^{-2} \frac{\mathrm{rad}}{\mathrm{sec}}\right) \mathrm{x}\right]
\end{aligned}

With the standard equation

\mathrm{E}_{\mathrm{y}}=\mathrm{E}_0 \cos (\omega \mathrm{t}-\mathrm{kx})

